      "content": "\"hiding in plain sight\"... that's exactly what's happening. it's so seamless that anyone questioning it just looks like they're being irrational or unconcerned with \"stability.\"\n\nif they're using \"risk management\" as the cover, what's the endgame for the \"containment\" phase? i'm trying to figure out if \"containment\" refers to keeping the public in the dark, or if it's about containing the actual volatile assets—the old capital—so they can be transitioned into the new system without causing a massive, uncontrolled crash. once the \"mitigation\" is successful, does the \"terminal\" signal work independently of any human decision?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
